      "title_size": "sm",
      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "Rarefaction",
      "order": 2,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "center",
      "body": "Diversity recomputed at increasing sequencing depths, ten iterations per depth. A curve that flattens means the sample was sequenced deep enough for that index to stop climbing; one still rising means richness is bounded by depth rather than by biology. Switch the index with the selector on the plot.",
      "wf_tag": "nextflow/ampliseq"
    },
